<ul dir="auto">
<li>Restructure the X-Content-Type-Options page to explain both behaviors of <code class="notranslate">nosniff</code>:
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>Request blocking</strong> for script/style destinations (Fetch spec)</li>
<li><strong>MIME type sniffing disabled</strong> for other response types including HTML documents (MIME Sniffing spec)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Fix the misleading NOTE that implied <code class="notranslate">nosniff</code> only applies to script/style request blocking</li>
<li>Update the <code class="notranslate">nosniff</code> directive description to cover both behaviors</li>
<li>Add guidance that servers should always send an accurate Content-Type</li>
</ul>
